From 03db9f6b17264084b7b423245a0727e8463f025f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 02:58:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/12] tools(armv80): rewrite LSE atomics of AArch64 ELF/PE
 binaries for ARMv8.0 CPUs

Each LSE instruction becomes a branch to its own load/store-exclusive stub with the same
ordering; LDAPR becomes LDAR. ELF gets the stubs in a PT_LOAD made from a PT_NOTE entry, or
in a new segment carrying a moved program header table; PE gets a new section, and in hybrid
ARM64EC/ARM64X images only the ARM code-map ranges are touched and the stubs are added to the
code map. tests/atomics.c covers all 63 forms, CASP, SP bases, flags and contention.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
